WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.070
In 597, Augustine of Canterbury
began a mission to the English.

2
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.870
For over 1,400 years, Christianity
shaped Britain's laws,

3
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.960
calendar and buildings.

4
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:16.830
Then, in 2021, the census
asked its voluntary question:

5
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.610
what is your religion?

6
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:23.730
For the first time, fewer than half of
people in England and Wales chose Christian.

7
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:28.300
Yet parish churches and cathedrals
still stand in almost every town.

8
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.790
So is Britain still Christian?

9
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.700
In this mission, you'll read three
censuses and track how belief has changed.

10
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.610
Then you will weigh up the evidence on
both sides of the claim that Britain is

11
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.300
no longer Christian.

12
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.830
Your mission: decide what it would mean
for Britain to be a Christian country,

13
00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.230
and judge the evidence.
